# Zeyla — shared team conventions

24-hour hackathon, 5 people working in parallel. These rules exist so two
people never edit the same lines. Read them before you touch anything.

## API shape

- Every API endpoint returns JSON in the shape:
  `{ success: boolean, data: object | null, error: string | null }`
  Use the `ok()` / `fail()` helpers in `apps/api/src/lib/respond.ts`; never
  hand-roll the envelope.
- Every backend route handler is async/await, wrapped in try/catch, never
  throws unhandled. Wrap handlers in `asyncHandler()` from the same file if
  you would rather not write the try/catch yourself.

## Secrets

- Never write a literal API key, secret, or private key into any committed
  file. Always read from `process.env` (backend goes through
  `apps/api/src/config/env.ts`; frontend uses `import.meta.env.VITE_*`).
- If a new secret is needed, add its name (not its value) to both
  `apps/api/.env.example` and `apps/web/.env.example` in the same commit.

## Folder ownership

- Do not edit files outside your owned folder (see `.github/CODEOWNERS`)
  without opening a PR and getting the owner to merge it.
- Do not edit `apps/api/src/app.ts` except to add or remove a single route
  registration line for your own module. No business logic, no route
  handlers, no middleware bodies live in that file.
- Same rule for `apps/web/src/App.tsx`: one `<Route>` line per page folder,
  nothing else.
- `apps/web/src/components/` and `packages/shared/` are shared. PR only.

## Database migrations

- Always `git pull` immediately before generating a new migration file, so
  migration numbers never collide across two people working at the same time.
- Migrations live in `apps/api/db/migrations/` as `NNN_description.sql` and
  are applied in sorted filename order. Never edit an existing migration that
  someone else has already run — add a new one.

## Commits and branches

- Commit messages: `[module] short description`
  e.g. `[escrow] add chapa webhook signature verification`
- Branches: `feat/<module>-<short-description>`
  e.g. `feat/escrow-chapa-webhook`, `feat/discovery-map-view`
- Branches are short-lived: merge within a couple of hours, not end of day.
  Push at least every 30-45 minutes even mid-feature, so conflicts stay small.

## Stack conventions

- TypeScript everywhere, ESM modules. Relative imports inside `apps/api` must
  carry the `.js` extension (`./config/env.js`), even though the source is
  `.ts` — that is a Node ESM requirement, not a typo.
- Types shared between API and web go in `packages/shared`, imported as
  `@zeyla/shared`. Do not duplicate a type on both sides.
- Prefer a `501 not_implemented` stub over a silent empty handler until a flow
  is real.
